Spark Core's abstraction is the **RDD — Resilient Distributed Dataset**: a distributed collection of objects that can be cached in memory across cluster nodes. An RDD is:

- **immutable** — operations create new RDDs, never change one;
- **resilient** and **fault-tolerant** — missing or damaged partitions can be recomputed after node failures;
- **distributed** — its data resides on multiple nodes;
- **lazily evaluated** — nothing is computed until it is needed;
- **cacheable / persistent** — it can be kept in memory or on disk.
